From 86473932d9340aaa1668573ec363b98cc552ee7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor Abbott <cwabbott0@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 26 Nov 2024 22:42:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/33] nir: Add generic pass for lowering intersection shaders

This is based off of the intel brw_nir_lower_intersection_shader pass,
with the following changes:

- Split the pass in two, in case a driver doesn't want to inline any-hit
  shaders but still wants the tracking done here.
- Instead of storing the intermediate distance and hit kind in
  driver-specific datastructures, store them in variables (which will
  eventually turn into registers) and then add a new
  commit_ray_intersection intrinsic to let drivers write into their
  opaque driver-specific datastructures, which will only be called once
  before terminating. This is more efficient and more easily abstracts
  the differences in implementation. Drivers only have to implement
  commit_ray_intersection and ignore_ray_intersection themselves.
