In the case where we run out of space to store values printed by the
shader, we can turn the buffer into a circular log in order to still see
the last messages printed out. In order to do this, we need to change
the format to make the buffer contain an offset instead of the raw iova,
and this also requires an extra scratch register for "print" to hold the
mask to "and" the offset with. The number of entries
must be a power of two so that we compute the offset with a simple
"and" instruction.

